    "finding": "The remedy moves active fraction from ~99% (no pathwayGain) to ~56-77% across every grid point tried, a real and large effect, but every point stays 4-10x over the 15% target, and overlapAB moves the WRONG way (0.47 -> 0.8-0.9) as otherGain drops, because the brain's excess excitability is not concentrated in edges whose target class is ALPN/Kenyon_Cell: baselineCurrent (0.03, added to every neuron every step regardless of any edge) and the amplified primary route itself (gain 5/2-3, i.e. 10-15x on the real odour signal) are enough on their own to recruit most KCs once real (non-noise) input arrives, and pathwayGain has no lever over baselineCurrent. Lowering otherGain below 0.3 buys little further reduction (a floor around 55-60%) while costing reliability/overlap. No grid point in this one search reaches the 5-15% active-fraction target; the gate's final verdict is FAIL. Per FR-008 and tasks.md's 'the gate decides the project', no Phase 4+ task may be started. See ADR 011 D36 (Rejected)."
